    {
      "topLeftX": 65,
      "topLeftY": 293,
      "bottomRightX": 745,
      "bottomRightY": 329,
      "content": "From the coefficients in (1), one can determine the possible range of values for the 2 color difference signals shown in (3):",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 336,
      "bottomRightX": 694,
      "bottomRightY": 356,
      "content": "\\[\n\\mathrm{E} ^ {\\prime} \\mathrm{B} - \\mathrm{E} ^ {\\prime} \\mathrm{Y} \\quad \\text { is   in   the   range } [ - 0. 8 8 6, + 0. 8 8 6 ] \\tag {5}\n\\]",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 113,
      "topLeftY": 361,
      "bottomRightX": 405,
      "bottomRightY": 381,
      "content": "\\[\n\\mathrm{E} ^ {\\prime} \\mathrm{R} - \\mathrm{E} ^ {\\prime} \\mathrm{Y} \\quad \\text { is   in   the   range } [ - 0. 7 0 1, + 0. 7 0 1 ]\n\\]",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 66,
      "topLeftY": 413,
      "bottomRightX": 664,
      "bottomRightY": 432,
      "content": "The next step is to normalize the 2 color difference so they occupy the full scale of  \\( [-0.5, +0.5] \\) .",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 438,
      "bottomRightX": 694,
      "bottomRightY": 458,
      "content": "\\[\n\\mathrm{E} ^ {\\prime} \\mathrm{Cb} = (0. 5 / 0. 8 8 6) (\\mathrm{E} ^ {\\prime} \\mathrm{B} - \\mathrm{E} ^ {\\prime} \\mathrm{Y}) \\tag {6}\n\\]",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 113,
      "topLeftY": 464,
      "bottomRightX": 361,
      "bottomRightY": 483,
      "content": "\\[\n\\mathrm{E} ^ {\\prime} \\mathrm{Cr} = (0. 5 / 0. 7 0 1) (\\mathrm{E} ^ {\\prime} \\mathrm{R} - \\mathrm{E} ^ {\\prime} \\mathrm{Y})\n\\]",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 66,
      "topLeftY": 489,
      "bottomRightX": 373,
      "bottomRightY": 509,
      "content": "where  \\( E'_{Cb} \\)  and  \\( E'_{Cr} \\)  are in the range [-0.5, +0.5].",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 65,
      "topLeftY": 541,
      "bottomRightX": 729,
      "bottomRightY": 579,
      "content": "In 8 bits, Y', Cb and Cr are derived by normalizing E'Y, E'Cb and E'Cr to [0, 255]. Note that Cb and Cr are signed shifted by 128 since E'Cb and E'Cr are in the range [-0.5, 0.5]. Including (6) leads to:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 584,
      "bottomRightX": 694,
      "bottomRightY": 603,
      "content": "\\[\n\\mathrm{Y} ^ {\\prime} = 2 5 5 \\mathrm{E} _ {\\mathrm{Y}} ^ {\\prime} \\tag {7}\n\\]",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 609,
      "bottomRightX": 593,
      "bottomRightY": 629,
      "content": "\\[\n\\mathrm{Cb} = 2 5 5 \\mathrm{E} _ {\\mathrm{Cb}} ^ {\\prime} + 1 2 8 = 2 5 5 \\times (0. 5 / 0. 8 8 6) (\\mathrm{E} _ {\\mathrm{B}} ^ {\\prime} - \\mathrm{E} _ {\\mathrm{Y}} ^ {\\prime}) + 1 2 8\n\\]",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 113,
      "topLeftY": 635,
      "bottomRightX": 593,
      "bottomRightY": 654,
      "content": "\\[\n\\mathrm{Cr} = 2 5 5 \\mathrm{E} _ {\\mathrm{Cr}} ^ {\\prime} + 1 2 8 = 2 5 5 \\times (0. 5 / 0. 7 0 1) (\\mathrm{E} _ {\\mathrm{R}} ^ {\\prime} - \\mathrm{E} _ {\\mathrm{Y}} ^ {\\prime}) + 1 2 8\n\\]",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
